WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.230
The H Q board: every guard at a glance, and what needs attention.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.070
The top row shows who's performing, who's on deck, and who's in the hole.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:14.610
Then every home room: free, assigned, in use, or cleared.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:23.610
Each card has the schedule times, where the guard and props are and how long ago, the home room, inspection, the guide, and the director.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:32.080
Once guard and props move together, it's one Unit chip. On the floor, it shows how far off the scheduled time they went on.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:38.883
Red means something is late, like a guard not at warm-up by its time. Amber means it's due soon.

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:46.050
The line in red says exactly what. Nothing is ever blocked; this is how H Q knows where to look.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:54.630
The director line shows check-in. Only roles with Director contact, like Contest H Q, see their number.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:02.307
The public board needs no sign-in. Send the link to the announcer or hospitality, or put it on a TV.

00:01:02.507 --> 00:01:09.150
It shows just the schools and where they are, with breaks and awards. No names, no phone numbers.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.920
Put the boards on a TV or tablet. They refresh by themselves every twenty seconds.
